      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 12 at 3:41AM HST until November 12 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI OAHU MOLOKAI AND NORTH FACING SHORES OF MAUI...\n\n.Surf from a large, north-northwest swell will maintain at near-\nwarning level this morning and will begin to decrease this\nafternoon. Surf is expected to start falling below advisory levels\nby tonight.\n\n* WHAT...For north-facing shores, surf 18 to 24 feet this morning,\nthen diminishing through the day. For west-facing shores, surf\n14 to 18 feet this morning, then diminishing through the day.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai, Oahu,\nMolokai and north facing shores of Maui.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
      "instruction": "Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't\ngo out.",
